[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **Direct Post-Cooling Delivery**: Once the object is cooled, navigate straight to the destination and place it without extraneous detours or re-searching.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   _Apply when: Right after the cooling action succeeds._
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **Enforce Cooling Before Placement**: Do not place the target object in its final location until you have successfully executed a cooling action with the fridge.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   _Apply when: When holding the correct object and before any placement action is attempted._
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **Phase-Ordered Plan**: Always execute clean tasks in the fixed sequence: 1) locate & acquire target object, 2) bring it to an available water source/sink to clean, 3) navigate to final location, 4) place object.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   _Apply when: As soon as the goal specifies the object must be clean before placement._
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **No Appliance Before Object**: Do not move to or interact with the microwave or final placement location until the target object is picked up, preventing wasted navigation steps.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   _Apply when: Whenever you are tempted to head to microwave/destination without holding the required object._
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **State Verification Before Drop**: Always inspect or infer the object’s state after cleaning; if still not confirmed clean, re-clean before final placement to satisfy goal conditions.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   _Apply when: Immediately after a cleaning action and before placing the object at its target location._
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m ### Mistakes to Avoid
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **Don't**: Agent repeatedly revisits the same already-searched locations or containers instead of exploring new ones.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   **Instead**: Maintain an exploration map that records which rooms/containers have been fully inspected and prioritize unvisited or unopened candidates until all reasonable options are exhausted.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **Don't**: Agent decides a closed container is empty without opening it, causing missed discoveries of target objects.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   **Instead**: Always open and inspect every plausible closed container at least once before ruling it out, using a checklist of unopened containers in the current room.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **Don't**: Agent ignores or walks away from target objects that are already visible and reachable.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   **Instead**: Embed a perception buffer that immediately queues pick-up actions for visible goal objects and interrupts any ongoing exploratory loop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **Don't**: Agent keeps searching after acquiring enough items because it loses track of how many targets have been collected.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   **Instead**: Maintain explicit numerical goals and increment/decrement them on every successful pickup or placement, triggering transition to the next sub-goal when counts are satisfied.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m - **Don't**: Agent fails to deliver a held target object to the known destination, instead continuing to wander.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=78284)[0m   **Instead**: Adopt a hierarchical policy that, upon holding a goal object, immediately switches to a high-priority ‘deliver-to-goal’ subtask before resuming further search.
